      "id": "quotient_cardinality",
      "dependencies": [],
      "spec": {
        "name": "M5.Period.quotient_cardinality",
        "statement": "∀ F : M5.BinaryPolynomial, F.Monic → Nat.card (AdjoinRoot F) = 2 ^ F.natDegree",
        "imports": [
          "M5Cardinality"
        ],
        "context": "",
        "queries": [
          "finite vector space cardinality",
          "orderOf finite monoid"
        ],
        "guidance": "Use Nat.card_congr ((AdjoinRoot.powerBasisAux' hF).equivFun.toEquiv), whose target is functions Fin F.natDegree → ZMod 2. Simplify the function-space Nat.card via Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_fun, Fintype.card_fin and ZMod.card. The degree-zero case is already covered by the empty-index basis; do not add F ≠ 1 or irreducibility. Return only tactic lines without a leading by."
      },
      "metadata": {
        "source_section": 5,
        "supports_obligation": "M5_PERIOD_BOUND",
        "scope": "finite_ring_cardinality_and_period_bound",
        "upstream_dependencies": [],
        "dependency_declarations": [],
        "fallback_queries": [
          "addition commutativity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "period_cardinality_bound",
      "dependencies": [
        "quotient_cardinality"
      ],
      "spec": {
        "name": "M5.Period.period_cardinality_bound",
        "statement": "∀ F : M5.BinaryPolynomial, F.Monic → F.coeff 0 = 1 → M5.signaturePeriod F ≤ 2 ^ F.natDegree",
        "imports": [
          "M5Cardinality"
        ],
        "context": "",
        "queries": [
          "finite vector space cardinality",
          "orderOf finite monoid"
        ],
        "guidance": "Install the local Finite (AdjoinRoot F) instance from accepted M5.Period.quotient_finite. Unfold M5.signaturePeriod and apply orderOf_le_card to AdjoinRoot.root F. Rewrite Nat.card with the accepted quotient_cardinality theorem. The coeff-zero assumption matches the original M5 signature domain; the estimate itself need not use it. Preserve ≤ 2^degree, including F=1. Do not add a strict inequality or a nonconstant restriction. Return only tactic lines without a leading by."
      },
      "metadata": {
        "source_section": 5,
        "supports_obligation": "M5_PERIOD_BOUND",
        "scope": "finite_ring_cardinality_and_period_bound",
